description.narrative:
General question: Results related to the intended outcome 2015Question: Summarise results related to the intended outcome (this information will be sent to Open Aid)Answer: As already highlighted in the reporting, out of the three objectives; 
- To support development of a Government Action Plan for the implementation and monitoring of the recommendations of the Committee on the Rights of the Child; 
- To support drafting of a Child Act which comprehensively promotes and protects the rights of children in Afghanistan through development of required
coordinated framework and; 
- To strengthen the capacity of the newly established Juvenile Police Units to deal and handle cases of children in contact with the law in a child friendly manner (as defined by UNICEF and other child care organisations.). 
None of the three objectives have completely been met.
No government action plan was developed, the drafting of a Child Act is delayed, the strengthening of the Juvenile Police Units has achieved limited results although a gap analysis has been made as well as a capacity building plan for the Juvenile Police produced.
